Seventeenth system tracing expansion (2026-10-13)
===============================================

14 new kernel contracts at 27 source sites in seven IPC source files. Five
profiles bring the bsdinstruments installation catalog to 434. Profiles use
the existing /usr/share/bsdinstruments/profiles base installation mechanism;
no installation was performed. The inventory is coverage-seventeenth.json.
All selectors are sdt:::NAME. A contract is a unique provider/module/function/
name tuple, not the number of call sites or loaded instances.

Purpose and safety
------------------
Existing pipe, shared-memory, kqueue and IPC lifecycle/wait probes do not
explain many failures. This pass adds causal pressure and limit events, plus
large-page retry and actual wait timing. A rejected resource request is not
proof of system-wide OOM. Successful fast paths gain no new event sites.
All new calls exclude cold startup. They use existing syscall/thread paths,
not early initialization, raw interrupt filters, allocators or panic handlers.
No allocation, extra locking, counter modification, payload or credential
collection is introduced. Supplied profiles do not dereference pointers.
Some probes execute under existing sleeping locks/mutexes; enabled tracing
there can extend lock hold time. No live overhead measurement is claimed.

Contracts (arguments in order)
-----------------------------
pipe-buffer-pressure: pipe identity, reason, attempted allocation bytes.
  1 = RLIMIT_PIPEBUF accounting rejected the reservation.
  2 = global pipe KVA reservation threshold rejected an unprivileged caller.
  3 = pipe_map virtual mapping failed.
Emits for failed attempts including attempts followed by SMALL_PIPE_SIZE
fallback. It does not by itself mean the pipe creation/resize ultimately failed.
pipe-buffer-retry: pipe identity, failed size, fallback size, immediately before
the existing small-buffer retry. Correlate with existing pipe resize results.

shmfd-swap-pressure: shmfd identity, additional requested swap reservation bytes.
This is swap/accounting reservation failure while extending ordinary shared
memory, not physical allocation failure or proof that all swap is full.
shmfd-largepage-pressure: shmfd, page-size index, retry count, allocation policy,
on contiguous-page allocation failure. Count is zero for the first failed
attempt and resets after each successfully allocated large page. Policy is
SHM_LARGEPAGE_ALLOC_*; failure may lead to EINTR, ENOMEM, reclaim or waiting.
shmfd-largepage-retry: shmfd, page-size index, retry count, before reclamation.
The event denotes an attempt, not recovery success or completed allocation.
shmfd-largepage-wait-start/done: shmfd (done adds vm_wait_intr error), immediately
around the interruptible sleep following an ENOMEM reclamation result.
The VM object lock is already released; the existing range lock keeps the
operation serialized. Partial large-page growth may survive a later failure.

sysvshm-limit: reason, requested bytes.
  1 = system segment-count limit (original, unrounded requested bytes).
  2 = system committed-page limit.
  3 = no free descriptor after attempting descriptor-table growth.
  4 = RACCT_NSHM rejection.
  5 = RACCT_SHMSIZE rejection.
Reasons 2--5 report page-rounded bytes; reasons 4--5 require active RACCT.
sysvshm-pager-pressure: page-rounded bytes, physical-pager selection boolean,
when vm_pager_allocate returns NULL. Does not expose keys or credentials.

sysvmsg-limit: reason (1 = no free queue descriptor; 2 = RACCT_NMSGQ rejection),
configured msgmni. msgmni is contextual system configuration, not the RACCT
limit or a measured current queue count. These events concern queue creation.
sysvsem-limit: reason, requested semaphore count.
  1 = system semaphore-element capacity exceeded.
  2 = no free semaphore-set descriptor.
  3 = RACCT_NSEM rejection.
These concern set creation, not every semop/undo allocation failure.

kqueue-timer-limit: knote identity, configured callout maximum, after reverting
the failed callout reservation during attach or fork copy. The maximum can be
changed concurrently and is contextual, not an exact snapshot of a counter.
kqueue-expand-pressure: kqueue, kind (1 = descriptor list; 2 = identifier hash),
allocation flags, when storage allocation returns NULL. No identifier payload
or stale pointer dereference is captured.
mqueue-count-limit: configured maxmq, when the existing queue-count comparison
rejects allocation. This is not malloc exhaustion; the subsequent allocation
uses M_WAITOK. maxmq can change concurrently. Only the active allocation path
is covered; disabled mqfs creation routines and an unreachable node-failure
branch were not instrumented.

Profiles
--------
pipe-buffer-pressure: failed attempts by cause/size and fallback sizes.
shm-largepage-pressure: swap reservation sizes, failed large-page attempts by
size index/policy, reclaim counts, actual wait latency and returned errors.
sysv-ipc-pressure: creation limits by cause and requested resources.
kqueue-resource-pressure: timer cap and storage allocation failures.
mqueue-count-pressure: queue-count rejections grouped by configured limit.

Start before the workload. The wait pair uses PID/TID/depth keys and clears
matched state. Dropped events invalidate pairing; elapsed time includes
scheduling. These profiles collect aggregates, not pointer identities, paths,
message contents, IPC keys or credentials. PID filters apply to initiating
threads. Existing lifecycle profiles remain useful for final operation results.

Validation
----------
Artifacts and exact originals: /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace-seventeenth-validation.
Maintained scripts in this directory:
  coverage-seventeenth-modules.py: native mqueue implementation module build.
  coverage-seventeenth-compile.py: seven sources, hooks on/off (14 compilations).
  coverage-seventeenth-check.py: source hashes, selector/arity checks, ten
    offline profile compiles (plain and PID/duration filtered), executable
    SDT NOP sites in enabled objects and absence in disabled objects.
  coverage-seventeenth-codegen.py: all seven no-hooks .text byte sequences
    match saved originals with diagnostic file/line macros normalized.
    This does not claim relocation equivalence or runtime qualification.
  coverage-seventeenth-linked.py: executable new site in linked mqueuefs.ko.
  coverage-seventeenth-variants.py: RACCT disabled in three System V IPC files,
    both hook modes (six compilations); only non-RACCT limit sites remain.
The prepared GENERIC-NODEBUG kernel is linked using -j16 and SRCTOP=/usr/src
under /usr/obj/usr/src/amd64.amd64/sys/GENERIC-NODEBUG. All compilation uses
available logical CPUs. Source edits are relative to saved current originals,
preserving earlier rounds and unrelated changes; session.patch reverse-checks.

No module load, forced OOM, limit mutation, installation, publication or reboot.
/dev/dtrace is unavailable: offline compilation and ELF checks do not prove
live firing or qualify enabled-trace overhead. Builds are native amd64, not
cross-architecture certification. Limits and failure paths were not induced.
